<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?><?xml-stylesheet href="http://www.blogger.com/styles/atom.css" type="text/css"?><feed xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom' xmlns:openSearch='http://a9.com/-/spec/opensearchrss/1.0/' xmlns:gd="http://schemas.google.com/g/2005"><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post3797340157791807920..comments</id><updated>2017-04-13T04:47:21.148-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Comments on Pro Libertate: When The State Owns Your Name</title><link rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#feed' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/feeds/comments/default'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/3797340157791807920/comments/default'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/when-state-owns-your-name.html'/><link rel="hub" href="http://pubsubhubbub.appspot.com/"/><author><name>William N. Grigg</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/14368220509514750246</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='32' height='19' src='http://3.bp.blogspot.com/-5rhFUXs_62I/VgVL2E3rMII/AAAAAAAAMJ4/cjJOyI7W208/s220/Photo%2BRon%2BPaul%2BLiberty%2BReport.jpg'/></author><generator version='7.00' uri='http://www.blogger.com'>Blogger</generator><openSearch:totalResults>9</openSearch:totalResults><openSearch:startIndex>1</openSearch:startIndex><openSearch:itemsPerPage>25</openSearch:itemsPerPage><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-2626878631386140682</id><published>2008-04-30T03:23:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2008-04-30T03:23:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>One of my buddy&#39;s recently got into some trouble a...</title><content type='html'>One of my buddy&#39;s recently got into some trouble at a bar and the short story is he was arrested on assault charges which are ridiculous we were there and watched as a random guy came up to him punched him in the face and began repeatedly beating him. He stood up to defend himself and in the crossfire the wasted dude fell and banged his head on the kerb. The cops show up and don&#39;t want to hear us and arrest him.&lt;BR/&gt;It all got cleared up in the end but had that have gone to court and my friend had to have paid &lt;A HREF=&quot;http://www.jwsuretybonds.com/list_court.htm&quot; REL=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;court bonds&lt;/A&gt; could he have claimed them back or even sued the police force for wrongful arrest? Also where would be the best place for &lt;A HREF=&quot;http://www.jwsuretybonds.com/surety_bond_types.htm&quot; REL=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;getting bonded&lt;/A&gt;?</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/3797340157791807920/comments/default/2626878631386140682'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/3797340157791807920/comments/default/2626878631386140682'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/when-state-owns-your-name.html?showComment=1209547380000#c2626878631386140682' title=''/><author><name>Anonymous</name><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/blank.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/when-state-owns-your-name.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-3797340157791807920' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/3797340157791807920' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-262634513"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="April 30, 2008 at 3:23 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-551382442988345837</id><published>2007-06-01T15:54:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2007-06-01T15:54:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Will, having taken a second look at the picture at...</title><content type='html'>Will, having taken a second look at the picture at the top where the guy has the gun drawn, I think it might be funnier if you replaced &#39;tyranny?&#39; with something like &quot;Got tyranny?&quot;</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/3797340157791807920/comments/default/551382442988345837'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/3797340157791807920/comments/default/551382442988345837'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/when-state-owns-your-name.html?showComment=1180734840000#c551382442988345837' title=''/><author><name>DrFix</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/13996714804361467430</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='32' height='32' src='http://www.visitrip.com/contact_files/agentsmith.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/when-state-owns-your-name.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-3797340157791807920' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/3797340157791807920' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-388975791"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="June 1, 2007 at 3:54 PM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-4634355881155007035</id><published>2007-06-01T12:34:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2007-06-01T12:34:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Zachary is correct, if one is a pedestrian, in sta...</title><content type='html'>Zachary is correct, if one is a pedestrian, in states that require one to identify oneself to a cop, all you need to do is give them your name, not show some state-approved form of ID. Of course, why this doesn&#39;t also hold for a driver is interesting. If the state requires one to hold a driver&#39;s license to drive on public highways (ask yourself: why should the state do this? After all, they don&#39;t require a license to ride a horse), why can&#39;t they then require a license to walk on public sidewalks? I predict that eventually they will try this tactic.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;For more details on conducting oneself with the cops, I recommend &lt;I&gt;You and the Police&lt;/I&gt;, by &lt;B&gt;Boston T. Party&lt;/B&gt;.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/3797340157791807920/comments/default/4634355881155007035'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/3797340157791807920/comments/default/4634355881155007035'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/when-state-owns-your-name.html?showComment=1180722840000#c4634355881155007035' title=''/><author><name>Anonymous</name><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/blank.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/when-state-owns-your-name.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-3797340157791807920' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/3797340157791807920' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-262634513"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="June 1, 2007 at 12:34 PM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-1392581827542624771</id><published>2007-05-31T08:53:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2007-05-31T08:53:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Saw the video.  Seems the guy wanted simply to kno...</title><content type='html'>Saw the video.  Seems the guy wanted simply to know why he was being asked to produce ID, questioned them whether he was blocking any traffic, and wouldn&#39;t submit because all he was getting in return was that they were doing an &quot;investigation&quot;.  How much more vague can a cop get with questions like that.  Besides, I&#39;m sick and tired of handing over ID everytime some yokel, cop or not, says they want it. By that very definition you&#39;re already guilty until &quot;proven&quot; innocent.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/3797340157791807920/comments/default/1392581827542624771'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/3797340157791807920/comments/default/1392581827542624771'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/when-state-owns-your-name.html?showComment=1180623180000#c1392581827542624771' title=''/><author><name>DrFix</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/13996714804361467430</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='32' height='32' src='http://www.visitrip.com/contact_files/agentsmith.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/when-state-owns-your-name.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-3797340157791807920' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/3797340157791807920' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-388975791"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="May 31, 2007 at 8:53 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-3436701464206087931</id><published>2007-05-30T08:23:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2007-05-30T08:23:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>If you are not driving, I thought you just have to...</title><content type='html'>If you are not driving, I thought you just have to give the officer your name in most states, not an ID. I was with someone in Colorado a few years ago and they were openly carrying a sidearm, for which no permit is necessary, only for concealment. An officer came up and asked for id, and my friend said &quot;no.&quot; The officer was taken aback but then asked for his name and my friend complied. He said that was the way it worked, id only required when driving.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/3797340157791807920/comments/default/3436701464206087931'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/3797340157791807920/comments/default/3436701464206087931'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/when-state-owns-your-name.html?showComment=1180534980000#c3436701464206087931' title=''/><author><name>Zachary</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/05334525584242029389</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/when-state-owns-your-name.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-3797340157791807920' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/3797340157791807920' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-995279443"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="May 30, 2007 at 8:23 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-7668855325963041912</id><published>2007-05-30T04:14:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2007-05-30T04:14:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Oh, those militarized and nationalized police! You...</title><content type='html'>Oh, those militarized and nationalized police! You can&#39;t live with &#39;em ....and you can&#39;t live with &#39;em!</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/3797340157791807920/comments/default/7668855325963041912'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/3797340157791807920/comments/default/7668855325963041912'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/when-state-owns-your-name.html?showComment=1180520040000#c7668855325963041912' title=''/><author><name>Anonymous</name><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/blank.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/when-state-owns-your-name.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-3797340157791807920' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/3797340157791807920' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-262634513"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="May 30, 2007 at 4:14 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-6651534275234408682</id><published>2007-05-30T00:33:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2007-05-30T00:33:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Note the contrast between Ross&#39;s snarling, feral v...</title><content type='html'>&lt;I&gt;Note the contrast between Ross&#39;s snarling, feral visage and the incredulous composure displayed by Greenwell, and ask yourself: Which of these two displays the civilized face of freedom?&lt;/I&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Indeed, the contrast is quite stark. That picture is worth a thousand words.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Great find, Will.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/3797340157791807920/comments/default/6651534275234408682'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/3797340157791807920/comments/default/6651534275234408682'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/when-state-owns-your-name.html?showComment=1180506780000#c6651534275234408682' title=''/><author><name>dixiedog</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/09845646940134894119</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='32' height='32' src='http://members.cox.net/ogdenwb/images/dixiedog1.jpg'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/when-state-owns-your-name.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-3797340157791807920' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/3797340157791807920' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-504942784"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="May 30, 2007 at 12:33 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-8985376718554230814</id><published>2007-05-30T00:09:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2007-05-30T00:09:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Hey Will, an idea just popped in me just to demons...</title><content type='html'>Hey Will, an idea just popped in me just to demonstrate how apathetic and complacent the &lt;I&gt;commoners&lt;/I&gt; REALLY are why don&#39;t we organize a &quot;Million Libertarian March&quot; or a &quot;Million Constitutionalist March&quot; and see what the turnout would be compared to, say, the &quot;Million Man March&quot; or &quot;Million Mom March&quot; (which demonstrated how fascist-minded many women REALLY are) were.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Hahahahaa!!! I&#39;d bet everything I own it&#39;d be miniscule by comparison. I&#39;d assert that there ain&#39;t a scant million &lt;I&gt;genuine&lt;/I&gt; libertarians (not libertines!) or &lt;I&gt;genuine&lt;/I&gt; constitutionalists in the  whole damn country.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Anyway, Venezuela&#39;s commoners (and their legislature and judicial branches of government) remind me much about our own respectively. They&#39;re only NOW becoming &lt;A HREF=&quot;http://corner.nationalreview.com/post/?q=ZDVhZjFkYzJiY2E2ZDU4MTA1YmY5MzJkY2U1YzJiZjk=&quot; REL=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;alarmed and think Chavez is becoming a dictator&lt;/A&gt;. He was already long ruling by decree and the legislature and judiciary are merely ornamental branches of their government tree.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;They wanted &quot;socialism or death&quot; and they got what they wanted, socialism. I guess they were ignorant of the fact that &quot;socialism&quot; is but &quot;communism lite&quot; or Trotsky&#39;s version rather than Stalin&#39;s. The Fourth International version.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Our commoners may only get riled up about what&#39;s happening long after it&#39;s way too late to reverse the course. It may already be too late, for that matter. And the irony, as well as the tragedy of it, would be that the people cried out and &lt;I&gt;voted&lt;/I&gt; for it! Just like the Germans managed in 1933 and Venezuelans accomplished in 1998. Could America be far behind? No.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Oh, and I&#39;ll say again that the Lizard Queen will be the next Prez, if Bush doesn&#39;t manage to put his &lt;A HREF=&quot;http://www.whitehouse.gov/news/releases/2007/05/20070517-6.html&quot; REL=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;latest executive order&lt;/A&gt; into action via &quot;natural and manmade disasters&quot; by January 20, 2009. That&#39;s a lot of time left for utilizing his own &quot;enabling act.&quot;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Anyway, back to Hillary, she&#39;s already stated recently that we need a &quot;shared prosperity&quot; society rather than an &quot;on your own&quot; variety.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Ominous signs, if you ask me.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/3797340157791807920/comments/default/8985376718554230814'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/3797340157791807920/comments/default/8985376718554230814'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/when-state-owns-your-name.html?showComment=1180505340000#c8985376718554230814' title=''/><author><name>dixiedog</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/09845646940134894119</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='32' height='32' src='http://members.cox.net/ogdenwb/images/dixiedog1.jpg'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/when-state-owns-your-name.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-3797340157791807920' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/3797340157791807920' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-504942784"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="May 30, 2007 at 12:09 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-5810564442997354553</id><published>2007-05-29T22:20:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2007-05-29T22:20:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>I can imagine what was going through the otherwise...</title><content type='html'>I can imagine what was going through the otherwise empty mind of the goon that was providing backup:&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&quot;I&#39;m from the government, and I&#39;m here to help.  Oh, my, a teenage girl!  Allow me to throw her to the ground and arrest her for no reason.  Guess I&#39;ve done my protecting and serving for the day!&quot;</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/3797340157791807920/comments/default/5810564442997354553'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/3797340157791807920/comments/default/5810564442997354553'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/when-state-owns-your-name.html?showComment=1180498800000#c5810564442997354553' title=''/><author><name>Jacob</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/03822812154321082569</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/when-state-owns-your-name.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-3797340157791807920' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/3797340157791807920' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-2013906820"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="May 29, 2007 at 10:20 PM"/></entry></feed>